From: Matt
Subject: [PATCH] bluetooth: hci_qca: pulse BT_EN low 50ms on ROME power-on

CAF drivers/bluetooth/bluetooth-power.c bt_configure_gpios(1) drives
the reset gpio low for 50 ms before releasing it; mainline only
raises bt_en. On the OnePlus 2 (QCA6174 ROME) the chip stays mute
(command 0xfc00 tx timeout) without the reset pulse.

--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
@@ -1870,6 +1870,12 @@
 	default:
 		qcadev = serdev_device_get_drvdata(hu->serdev);
 		if (qcadev->bt_en) {
+			/* CAF bluetooth-power.c bt_configure_gpios(1): drive the
+			 * reset gpio low for 50 ms before releasing it — ROME
+			 * chips need the pulse to start.
+			 */
+			gpiod_set_value_cansleep(qcadev->bt_en, 0);
+			msleep(50);
 			gpiod_set_value_cansleep(qcadev->bt_en, 1);
 			/* Controller needs time to bootup. */
 			msleep(150);
